The environment menu, and Stop sandbox in the sidebar.

The monitor icon left of the permission picker opened a menu that only named
the host. For a sandbox session it now opens EnvironmentMenu: a header with
the provider, the Pod's tailnet name and its state (Running, Idle, Stopped,
Starting or Failed, with a matching dot on the trigger), then rows for the
agent (working, or idle and when it exits), the Pod (uptime with the CPU and
memory it uses, or when it stopped), the VM disk (used of total, with a bar
that turns amber at 80% and red at 90%, as the kubelet counts free space, and
a warning at red) and when the idle Pod stops, or the start-up steps, or why
the start failed. While open it polls GET /v1/sessions/{id}/environment every
5 seconds (useSessionEnvironment); rows appear once their data has loaded.

Its actions: Copy SSH command; Keep running (Usual idle timeout, For 2 hours,
For 8 hours, Until I stop it, ticking the choice in force, saved with PUT
.../environment/keep-running; not offered once the agent has exited, since its
runner is what keeps the Pod; on a phone its choices replace the menu, with a
Back row, since a flyout beside the menu would open off the screen); Restart
agent (stop_session, keeps the Pod); Start agent when the agent has exited but
the Pod is up; Stop sandbox (the shared StopSandboxDialog); Start now
(stopped) and Try again (failed), which need a resumable host; Cancel start
while a stopped sandbox wakes; and Copy error details. Start now, Try again
and Start agent use retry_session, which wakes a resumable host or starts the
runner on a live one without adding anything to the transcript. The state
comes from the session's launch stage, its liveness and whether a turn is
running; after an action the menu shows where it's heading until the ~10s
liveness poll catches up. Controls are greyed out for anyone but the session's
owner, and in read-only sessions. A new sandbox session shows the menu while
it launches, before its host is bound. Sessions on other hosts, and on sandbox
providers other than agent_sandbox, keep upstream's menu. Spacing is scoped to
.environment-menu in index.css: every block sits 16px from the menu edge or
the nearest divider, and labels use text-box trimming so icons line up with
their capitals. agent_sandbox is named "Agent Sandbox" instead of
"Agent_sandbox Sandbox".

The sidebar's Stop session becomes Stop sandbox for sandbox sessions: it sends
stop_session with suspend_sandbox, so the Pod stops too, and confirms with
"Stop the sandbox?". It stays while the Pod is up after the agent exits.
Sessions on other hosts keep Stop session. The subscription tag's switch hint
points at Restart agent, which keeps the Pod and is enough to pick up another
account.
Pairs with the server patch 0015-environment-menu.patch.
Applies after 0019-project-repositories.patch. Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).
